## Testing strategy

- One Vitest lane (jsdom). `obsidian` resolves to the test double in
  `tests/__mocks__/obsidian.ts`; `tests/setup.ts` polyfills Obsidian's
  `HTMLElement` helpers (`createEl`, `empty`, …). Extend both as you use more
  API surface.
- Services get plain unit tests. Components mount with `@vue/test-utils` and a
  **partial plugin double provided under the real `PLUGIN_KEY`** — see
  `tests/vue/HomePage.test.ts` for the pattern.
- The mock `Modal` attaches to `document.body` on open, so dialog flows are
  testable with DOM queries; the mock `Notice` logs to `__noticeLog`.
- TDD: failing test first in the mirrored `tests/` path, then the
  implementation, then refactor.

## Adding a feature (checklist)

1. Model state/events first: extend settings (`withDefaults` keeps old vaults
   safe) and `AppEvents` if other surfaces must react.
2. Put logic in `src/core/` (unit-tested), rendering in `src/ui/`.
3. Register commands/views in `main.ts` — command ids never contain the plugin
   id or the word "command"; names are sentence case without the plugin name.
4. User feedback goes through `plugin.notices` / `plugin.modals`.
5. Style via `src/styles.css` (Obsidian CSS variables, no `!important`) or
   scoped SFC styles.
6. Run the local gate set before pushing (see `CLAUDE.md`).

## Constraints worth remembering

- {{mobileLine}}
- Build artifacts (`main.js`, `styles.css`) are generated — never edit or
  commit them; `src/styles.css` is the stylesheet source.
- `manifest.json`/`versions.json` change only through `npm version` (the
  `sync-version` script) — `check:artifacts` fails on desync.
- Ratchets (`check:loc`, `check:css`, `check:quality`, coverage floors) only
  tighten: lock improvements in with each gate's `--update` in the same PR.
